  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to a Consolidated Law-Enforcement and Policy Response to Trafficking in Persons in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to the enhancement of the government&#x2019;s efforts in efficiently investigating and prosecuting trafficking in persons (TiP), as well as in developing and coordinating policies against TiP and is line with the national anti-TiP priorities of the Moldovan Government as listed in the National Anti-TiP Strategy 2018-2023, SDG Targets 5.2,8.7 and 16.2 of SDGs, and in meeting the corresponding JTiP and GRETA reports&#x2019; recommendations. The project will address chiefly the current gaps in the Moldovan law-enforcement institutional framework, thus contributing to strengthening the capacity of the Center for Combatting Trafficking in Persons of the Ministry of Interior, Prosecutor General&#x2019;s Office, judges specialized on TiP cases, also aiming at enhancing the interaction of these main law-enforcement structures in order to improve the prosecution of the TiP crime in Moldova. In addition, the project will contribute to the development of the National Referral Mechanism for victims of crimes protection and consolidation of TiP related policy at the national level.</narrative>
  </description>
